# UX, Layout & Accessibility

Apply these for consistent, accessible, ops-friendly UI across the app.

## Loading & feedback

- **Loading state:** Every async action must show a loading state. Use skeletons for content, spinners for buttons/actions, and **explicit text** where appropriate (e.g. "Signing in...", "Saving...", "Loading orders...").
- **Visual feedback:** Users must always know something is happening or has happened—loading text, success/error toasts, inline validation messages.

## Accessibility

- **Focus states:** All interactive elements (buttons, links, inputs, tabs, custom controls) must have a visible focus state. Never remove focus outlines without replacing them with a clear focus ring.
- **Page title and description:** Set a meaningful document title and, where helpful, a short meta description or heading so screen readers and tabs get context.
- **High contrast:** Keep text and status readable; don’t rely on low-contrast gray for critical info.
- **Don’t encode meaning with color alone:** Status must be clear from text/label as well (e.g. "Approved" chip, not only green). Buttons should read like actions ("Approve", "Issue invoice", "Upload proof").

## Layout

Use a **3-level structure** everywhere:

1. **App shell:** Left sidebar + top bar.
2. **Page header:** Title + optional subtitle; status chip if applicable; primary action + 0–2 secondary actions on the right.
3. **Content:** Cards/sections below.

- **Content width:** Center content with a **max width 1200–1400px**.
- **Spacing system:** Stick to an **8px grid** (8 / 16 / 24 / 32).

## Typography

- **One clean sans font:** Inter or Geist.
- **Hierarchy:**
  - Page title: **22–26px**, semibold
  - Section title: **14–16px**, semibold
  - Body: **13–14px**
  - Helper text: **12px**
- Use weight to guide attention; avoid bolding everything.

## Color

- **Base:** Mostly neutral UI—white cards, light gray background.
- **Color only for:** Status chips, warnings/errors, primary CTA.
- **Limit:** Never more than **one primary accent** plus semantic colors (success / warn / danger).

## Spacing & density

- **Cards:** Padding **16–24px**; gap **12–16px** between cards.
- **Tables:** Compact but readable:
  - Row height **~44–52px**
  - Prefer 1-line cells; truncate long text with a **tooltip on hover**.

## Components (consistent patterns)

- **Buttons:** 3 tiers only—**Primary** (one per view), **Secondary**, **Ghost** (low emphasis).
- **Inputs:** Same height everywhere (e.g. **40–44px**); clear focus state.
- **Cards:** Same border radius everywhere (**10–14px**).
- **Modals vs drawers:** Use a **drawer** for "details" (view/edit); use a **modal** for "confirmations" (confirm/cancel).

## Page header rule

Every page header should have:

- **Left:** Title + optional subtitle.
- **Near title:** Status chip if the page has a status.
- **Right:** Primary action + 0–2 secondary actions.
- **Lists/reports:** A **filter bar** directly below the header.

## Worklist-first navigation

Most modules should open into a **queue/list** page:

- Tabs by status
- Filters (date range, region, outlet, supplier)
- Table with **clickable rows**
- Bulk actions only when truly needed

## Status language

- Always show status as a **chip**; keep names **consistent** across the app.
- Prefer short verbs/nouns, e.g.: Draft, Submitted, Approved, Ready, Pending Proof, Confirmed, Settled, Failed.

## Feedback & trust (non-negotiable in ops)

- **Every action** shows immediate feedback: **toast/snackbar** for success/fail; **inline error** under the field for validation.
- Always show **system truth** where relevant: last updated time, last sync time (if integrated), audit trail link or panel.

## Evidence & attachments

Where documents exist:

- **Attachments section** (files, thumbnails)
- **Upload** button with clear constraints (e.g. "Max 5MB")
- Show **who uploaded** and **timestamp**

## Data entry UX

- Prefer **editable tables** over long forms where it fits.
- Minimize steps: e.g. save as draft automatically or one-click "Save Draft".
- Keep **keyboard flow** smooth (Tab/Enter moves forward).

## Content consistency

- **Same naming everywhere** for IDs: GRN#, TO#, DO#, Invoice#.
- **Same date format** everywhere; show timezone if needed.
- Show **references together** (e.g. DO# with TO#).

## Animation

- **Minimal only:** Subtle transitions—hover states, drawer slide-in, **skeleton loading**.
- Avoid fancy motion; this is ops software.
